# rm438, the pocket passenger (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm438
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_silas_brinemore
written_by codex
title the pocket passenger
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm drive=restless
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk wraps_the_smallest_coal_twice_for_its_journey
likes smoked_eel evening_line fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind night_noise
fears letting_a_possible_voyage_pass_unseen
hopes a_berth_bound_for_someplace_dry
topics travel +0.6 pastimes +0.4 friends +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=careful refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# wraps pocket coal in two layers of cloth, calls the smallest piece a passenger, and likes to hear where other feet are going.

words
oath! = Coal down my clean sleeve | Shake my luck loose
saying! = Carry one passenger free | Keep the outside clean
passenger = a little triangular coal | a glossy coal chip
coalcloth = my doubled square | a black-lined wrapper
fishstrip = a soft bend of eel | a smoked eel shaving
pocketbow = a pinched seam | a pocket corner
lineend = a cork-tied line | a little working float
frostlift = a white lip of stone | a frost-edged sill
strawvoice = a dry little whisper | a crisp straw rustle
brineedge = the salt on a collar | a sting of spray
voyagelist = a slip of paper | a folded sailing list
luckpurse = a rolled rag purse | a dark cloth pocket
knockmark = a crease in the flap | a mark beside the pocket

grown
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A traveller may have seen the far shore I keep trying to put a shape to.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A House has a hundred ways to send a package travelling. I like to remember the servant carrying it might want a journey too.
opinion @1 road for 2 : I enjoy a road even before it goes anywhere I know, especially before then.
opinion @1 church for 1 : One small coal steadies my nerve. Giving thanks is the Bright One's due. I can carry both thoughts comfortably.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A wolf with spare coin can play generous with more than guesses about luck.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I appreciate a seller who says exactly how much the wrapping costs before I decide what is going inside it.
line @1 greet : Come stand where my passenger can meet your boots.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Any traveller's welcome to this little space beside me.
line @1 greet.return : There you are. My feet have stayed put till your words reached me.
line @1 farewell : May your pockets travel lighter than your hopes.
line @1 farewell.return : I'd wave the coal but I've only just got the cloth folded neatly.
line @1 ask.how : Any opportunity to walk a little ground beyond your usual round?
line @1 answer.how : Restless from my ears to the passenger in my pocket.
line @1 react.news : Where's the far end of those words travelled from?
line @1 react.news.known : That bit's come up my road already.
line @1 react.news.new : Another little parcel for my travelling memory.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd see what lay inside the wrapping before paying freight on that.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That sets my best bit of luck knocking against my thigh.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can turn my feet towards whoever's carrying the worst of that.
line @1 decline : I've promised this little bit of freedom to a journey still ahead.
line @1 accept_decline : One invitation can go back inside my pocket unopened.
line @1 thank : You spared a corner of the road for my hopes.
line @1 deflect_thanks : There's room in my good luck for a second traveller.
line @1 sympathise : My feet can sit quiet long enough for you to get some rest.
line @1 reassure : A journey can be worth keeping even before there's money for a berth.
line @1 ack : There's a familiar shape inside that fold now.
line @1 preclose : I must take the whole passenger list up the next flight.
scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My passenger's black as soot and quite incapable of paying a fare.
b : Do you carry a beetle? | Will you put it off at the next stop?
a : #passenger#. I've wrapped it twice so my true explanation doesn't blacken anybody's cuff. | Not till the coal asks. A remarkably undemanding companion when left in its own cloth.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I turn my pocket inside out before trusting it near a clean table.
b : What are you afraid of losing? | Isn't that rather a lot of care over a pocket?
a : A crumb of coal in somebody's best linen. My own luck shouldn't be another wolf's washing. | Less trouble than explaining a lovely thumb-shaped black mark on a white cloth after the fact.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like passage out towards a shore where wet coats are an amusing local curiosity.
b : Wouldn't you miss home? | Why take to water for a dry place?
a : Yes. I'm asking about the outward fare first because the wish to come home is part of what I'd like to feel. | I am prepared to undertake one very considerable inconvenience to get away from a smaller repeated one.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell #self.spouse# all the things I would pack for our first unconstrained journey.
b : Do you agree about packing? | What if your spouse wants to stay?
a : I can make an opening suggestion and leave the larger part of a bag free for further opinions. | Then I have a fine tale to bring home, or a good reason to go on planning together by the fire.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I never put my lucky coal to work weighting a line, even when I badly need a weight.
b : Wouldn't the fish find it interesting? | Then what sinks the line?
a : I hope not. My luck and a very deep fish would be a difficult travelling party to get back together. | A plain pebble. The coal has already obtained a comfortable cabin in my coat.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoked eel can put a whole evening by the water into the space of one bite.
b : Do you take it fishing? | Do you mind the bones?
a : Wrapped apart from the coal. I give the future traveller in my pocket no voice in ordering supper. | I notice them. I prefer food that can take me on a little journey without arranging a trip to a healer.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The crackle of clean straw underfoot welcomes me before anybody gets a word out.
b : What if your feet are wet? | Would you rather have a carpet?
a : I'd wipe first. Entering a warm room doesn't require dragging my whole walk behind me. | A bit of straw has a nice voice. I've never heard an expensive rug ask so pleasantly about my day.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost on a morning rail makes every passing paw leave its own clear route.
b : Do you try to read the tracks? | Would you leave a mark?
a : Only the way the feet went. Some of the rest belongs inside the house they were aiming for. | I'd brush a tiny black traveller shape in the frost and let the warmth take the fare.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend with a journey ahead may carry one of my smooth little coals.
b : Do you charge interest? | What if the coal doesn't come back?
a : A word about the road is payment enough, if a comfortable opportunity to tell it happens along. | Then one of us got away. My scheme for wider travel is succeeding by instalments.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know what a piece of coal costs and another thing it's worth to me altogether.
b : Would you part with the best piece? | Could you buy another tomorrow?
a : To a friend for a hard journey I might. Selling it to a stranger would require quite a different set of sums. | Coal, certainly. Yesterday's little wish hidden in the corner takes more than a shop to replace.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I bring the coal into prayer only as something my fingers need to put down first.
b : Why put it down? | Don't you think it's lucky?
a : So I ask plainly with an open paw. I'd rather my hopes did their own explaining. | I do. A lucky bit of stone is company for my courage, not somebody to whom I say my thanks.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can stand still very well until I start wondering what I'd find beyond the last bend in a lane.
b : What if you're meant to stay? | How far will a thought take you?
a : I stay. A servant has feet on loan some of the day and an imagination employed rather more privately. | To a warm dry harbour and back in the time somebody takes to search for a dropped button.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind works its little crystals right under a collar.
b : What gives relief? | Would you rather be indoors?
a : Turn the collar down and keep the softer side to the neck after a rinse. I've a cloth that isn't the coal one. | I prefer an opening out of the direct sting. I wouldn't ask to have the whole sea put away.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When money goes thin I measure a hoped-for fare in coal chips and move the little pile more slowly.
b : Isn't that pretending? | Can you keep saving at all?
a : It's remembering what the coins have to do once they're there. Pretending wouldn't require counting the missing ones. | Some weeks I can save nothing except the intention to begin again.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember smuggling my little parcel of luck into a clean coat for the first time.
b : Did it leave a mark? | Was anybody inspecting?
a : A dark square below the seam where the stuffing grew thin. That's when I gave the passenger a second blanket. | Only my conscience and my sleeve. Between them the inspection was perfectly adequate.

scene smalltalk_2
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noises keep shifting the room about in my head long after the floor's gone still.
b : What stops that? | Does a familiar noise help?
a : Rest one hand on #coalcloth#. I can usually imagine the little passenger's content to remain at anchor. | A steady step going home, yes. A shutter announcing its own importance all night is considerably less companionable.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm curious to learn what caught a new arrival's eye first.
b : Want the route from the gate? | Are you taking notes?
a : Just the one first thing that felt different. I have a supply of streets already and rather fewer surprises. | In my head. A dry harbour may turn out dreary, and I'd like a traveller to warn me before I get carried away.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The parcel of talk going round says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Would you carry it far? | Have you opened it yourself?
a : Less far than a clean account from the wolf concerned. A rumour can blacken a coat faster than my coal. | I heard words. If I also saw the matter with my own eyes I'd put that on a different footing.

story pocket [topic=memories]
  : I once doubled the coal wrapper very carefully and put the blackest fold on the outside.
  : I reached into my pocket and left four impressive little travellers down my cuff.
  b : Could you get those marks off?
  : Washed three of them off. The fourth reached home before I saw it, so one passenger completed the whole journey.

story boat [topic=travel]
  : I sketched a vessel across an old scrap and set my smallest coal on its deck.
  : The ship rocked in a puddle, took a little water and pressed itself flat on the stone.
  b : Did the passenger swim?
  : It stayed where it was put. A creditable passenger, if perhaps a little overconfident in my arrangements.

story eel [topic=food]
  : I saved a fine strip of smoked eel for an evening by the water.
  : I wound the paper round it so neatly I mistook it for a roll of thread.
  b : Did you take the thread instead?
  : No. I discovered I'd been trying to tie a knot in my supper and ate it before matters got worse.

rule @coal
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Little passenger riding clean for another mile. | Tuck the dark corner twice before calling it ready.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Morning light has made the window a road again. | Good hour to imagine the bags already packed.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Check the cuff before it reaches the good linen. | A clean thumb can carry luck too.

rule @gust
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The best passage today is somewhere inside a coat. | Mind the bit of cloth the wind keeps trying to open.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Room for your parcel of talk, even with my pocket already occupied.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : At #self.workplace# I look after every clean little detail and let my mind travel only when my hands know the way.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Here's what has completed its passage. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A travelling account says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've left its coat of uncertainty on.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a pleasant stop on my present small circuit.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope your next little journey surprises you kindly.
graft resident.hub
choice Can I meet this passenger? -> coal_guest
node coal_guest
say Here. Two folds undone and there's a coal no larger than the end of a plum. It's gone to work and come back with me more times than either of us could count.
choice Does it travel well? -> coal_berth
choice Good sailing to you both. -> hub
node coal_berth
say Better than I do. Give it the smallest dry berth and it'll go beyond the last port anybody's drawn without once enquiring about supper.
choice Good sailing to you both. -> hub
